url: "https://the-poverty-dispute.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the Franciscan poverty dispute, 1316-1329,
  built from public-domain editions with the original beside a working
  English translation, every excerpt read against the page images: the
  decretals Exiit qui seminat and Exivi de paradiso and the five decretals
  of John XXII (Friedberg 1881); Bernard Gui's sentences against four
  Beguins (Limborch 1692) and his Practica on the Beguins (Douais 1886);
  the order's chronicle (Analecta Franciscana II, 1887); Michael of
  Cesena's appeal of Avignon (Baluze-Mansi III, 1762); Dante's Paradiso XI
  (Moore 1904, Longfellow 1867); the appeal of Sachsenhausen (MGH
  Constitutiones V, 1909-13); Ockham's Opus nonaginta dierum (Goldast
  1614); and Angelo Clareno's Historia septem tribulationum (Ehrle 1886).
  With a timeline, a Compare page on fifteen questions, and an explicit
  list of what is not carried and why, above all Olivi's own writings.
  Companion game: Nec in communi.
